A window (whatever that would be in a tty text interface) that pops up
is a nightmare. There are OSes out there which I avoid also because of
the popping up windows that interrupt my work and distract my attention
from the task I work on; I want that kind of interruption neither in my
work nor in my play.

> Am I the only one that has this problem?  Actually my brother has the
> same problem, so does this problem just run in my family?

No. I suppose there are a lot who have problems, but to a different
degree. Attention in certain cases, watching the status line carefully,
are key (meta-)skills in Nethack.

The problems you describe are partly alleviated by the menu-color patch
which is available if you play on NAO. I'd also welcome if that patch
would be extended by highlighting other critical status messages, like
fainting or ill.[*]

